{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0\fswiss Arial;}{\f1\froman Times New Roman;}}\viewkind4\uc1\pard\f1\fs28\b Integrated Assignment\par\pard\f1\fs22\b Developing a Server Side application using Node & Express\par\pard\f1\fs20\par Instructions to use the project file provided:\par\pard\f1\fs20\bullet Read the problem statement, examples and the other details provided carefully and implement the solution\par\bullet Download the project FBWebService_Practice into your system and unzip it\par\bullet Install node_modules using the command npm install and start your server\par\bullet Ensure a local MongoDB instance is running before you start the server or run npm test\par\bullet Once the server started successfully, hit the URL http://localhost:1060/setupDb (GET request) to setup your database with initial set of documents\par\bullet Run index.html inside parserModule in live server to verify your code. Your application should not have any run-time/compilation errors for successful verification\par\bullet DO NOT alter the function name or the argument list of the function that is provided to you\par\bullet DO NOT add any new functions apart from the one given in the file where you write the solution\par\bullet DO NOT write codes that result in infinite loops/infinite recursive calls, because it just won't work!\par\pard\f1\fs24\b\par Problem Description:\par\pard\f1\fs20 EventXperience wants to automate the process of event ticket booking and management for which they want the implementation of the following.\par\pard\f1\fs20\bullet Book tickets for an event\par\bullet View all bookings for all events\par\bullet View all bookings done for a particular event\par\bullet View all bookings done by a particular customer\par\bullet Update the booking of a customer\par\pard\f1\fs24\b\par In FBWebService_Practice Folder:\par\pard\f1\fs20\b model/eventBooking.js:\b (Implemented)\par This file contains a Class EventBooking, which converts a generic object to EventBooking object\par\pard\f1\fs20\b utilities/requestlogger.js\b (Implemented)\par This file consists of a middleware function which logs all the requests made by the users into a text file RequestLogger.txt.\par\pard\f1\fs20\b utilities/connection.js\b (Implemented)\par This file contains the database schemas and a connection object\par The connection object has the following two methods to establish connection with the database:\par\bullet getCustomerCollection() 
 gives model object of Customer collection\par\bullet getEventCollection() 
 gives model object of Event collection\par\pard\f1\fs20 The database consists of the following two schemas:\par\bullet Customer: customerId, customerName, walletAmount, customerType (enum: Platinum/Gold/Silver)\par\bullet Event: eventId, eventName, basePricePerSeat, availableSeats, eventDate, status (enum: Scheduled/Cancelled/Expired), bookings (array of EventBooking sub-documents: customerId, bookingId, seatZone, quantity, bookingCost)\par\pard\f1\fs20\b model/dbsetup.js:\b (Implemented)\par This file contains the initial set of data for the collection and a method to insert the data into the respective collection in database.\par\pard\f1\fs20\b utilities/errorlogger.js:\b (To be implemented)\par This file contains a function errorLogger which should log the full stack trace of the error that may get thrown during execution of the program\par If there is some error in the code the entire error stack should be appended to the ErrorLogger.txt file with the timestamp of when the error had occurred\par If there is any error in appending the error to the ErrorLogger.txt, it should display the message "Failed in logging error" in console\par If error object's status property is set, then the response status should be set to error object's status value\par Else, the response status should be set to 500 and the error message should be sent as a JSON in the given format {"message" :<<message>>}\par errorLogger should be exported as a module\par\pard\f1\fs20\b utilities/validator.js:\b (To be implemented)\par This file contains a Validator object with three methods i.e. validateEventId, validateSeatZone and validateBookingId\par\pard\f1\fs20\b validateEventId\par This method should accept eventId as a parameter and validate it\par It should check if the eventId matches the following pattern:\par <<part1>>-<<part2>>\par part1 -> EVT\par part2 -> three digits (where first digit cannot be 0)\par e.g. EVT-101\par If the validation fails, it should throw an error with message "Error in event Id" after setting error status as 406\par\pard\f1\fs20\b validateSeatZone\par This method should accept seatZone as a parameter and validate it\par It should check that the seatZone is exactly one of: VIP, Standard, Economy\par If the validation fails, it should throw an error with message "Error in seat zone" after setting error status as 406\par\pard\f1\fs20\b validateBookingId\par This method should accept bookingId as a parameter and validate it\par It should check that the bookingId should always be of 4 digits only\par If the validation fails, it should throw an error with message "Error in booking Id" after setting the error status as 406\par\pard\f1\fs20\b model/events.js:\b (partially implemented)\par Instance of connection module is created by importing it\par This file contains eventBookingDb object with the following methods:\par\bullet generateId()\par\bullet checkCustomer()\par\bullet checkBooking()\par\bullet checkAvailability()\par\bullet bookTickets()\par\bullet getAllBookings()\par\bullet customerBookingsByEvent()\par\bullet getBookingsByEventId()\par\bullet updateCustomerWallet()\par\bullet updateBooking()\par Note: Details of the mentioned methods are given in the next section\par Finally, eventBookingDb object is exported as a module\par\pard\f1\fs20\b eventBookingDb.generateId():\b (Implemented)\par This method generates unique booking Ids for each new document that gets inserted\par The generated bookingId is returned wrapped inside a promise\par\pard\f1\fs20\b eventBookingDb.checkCustomer():\b (to be implemented)\par This method should take customerId as a parameter and check whether customer with given customerId exists or not\par A connection should be established to the database by invoking the getCustomerCollection method of the connection object\par It should fetch the customer details from Customer collection for the given customerId\par If the customer detail exists, it should return the customer object\par Else, it should return null\par\pard\f1\fs20\b eventBookingDb.checkBooking():\b (to be implemented)\par This method should take bookingId as a parameter and check whether booking with given bookingId exists or not\par A connection should be established to the database by invoking the getEventCollection method of the connection object\par It should fetch the Event details from Event collection for the given bookingId\par If the booking exists for the given bookingId, return the corresponding event object in which the booking is done\par Else, it should return null\par\pard\f1\fs20\b eventBookingDb.checkAvailability():\b (to be implemented)\par This method should take eventId as a parameter and check whether event with given eventId exists or not\par A connection should be established to the database by invoking the getEventCollection() method of the connection object\par It should fetch the event detail from Event collection for the given eventId\par If an event object for the given eventId is found, it should return the event object\par Else, it should return null\par\pard\f1\fs20\b eventBookingDb.updateCustomerWallet():\b (to be implemented)\par This method should accept customerId and bookingCost as parameters and update the wallet amount of the customer\par A connection should be established to the database by invoking the getCustomerCollection() method of the connection object\par It should update the wallet amount for the given customerId by decreasing the bookingCost\par On successful updation, return true\par Else, return false\par\pard\f1\fs20\b eventBookingDb.bookTickets():\b (to be implemented)\par This method should accept an eventBooking Object as a parameter, book the tickets for the customer, update the number of seats available for the event and the walletAmount of the customer\par A connection should be established to the database by invoking the getEventCollection method of the connection object\par It should invoke generateId method of eventBookingDb to generate unique booking Id\par A new document should be added to the bookings of Event collection with the values of customerId, bookingId, seatZone, quantity, bookingCost\par If new document is added successfully, update the number of seats available in the Event collection for the corresponding eventId\par It should also check for successful updation of seats available in the Event collection\par If successfully updated, it should update the corresponding customer's wallet amount by invoking updateCustomerWallet method that takes customerId and bookingCost as parameters\par If the wallet amount is updated for the customer, it should return the bookingId. Else, it should throw an error with message "Wallet not updated" after setting the error status as 502 (Bad gateway)\par Else, if the seats available for the event does not get updated, it should throw an error with message "Seats not updated" after setting the error status as 502 (Bad gateway)\par Else, it should throw an error with message "Booking failed" with status 500\par\pard\f1\fs20\b eventBookingDb.getAllBookings():\b (to be implemented)\par This method should not take any parameter and return all the bookings made in all the events\par A connection should be established to the database by invoking the getEventCollection method of the connection object\par It should fetch all bookings from all the events\par It should return an array of booking objects\par If no bookings are found, return null\par\pard\f1\fs20\b eventBookingDb.customerBookingsByEvent():\b (to be implemented)\par This method should take customerId and eventId as a parameter and return an array of all the bookings made by the customer in the given event\par A connection should be established to the database by invoking the getEventCollection method of the connection object\par It should fetch all the bookings made by a customer for the given eventId\par If bookings are found, it should return the same array of bookings object\par Else, it should return null\par\pard\f1\fs20\b eventBookingDb.getBookingsByEventId():\b (to be implemented)\par This method should take eventId as a parameter and return all the bookings made in that event\par A connection should be established to the database by invoking the getEventCollection() method of the connection object\par It should fetch only the bookings detail from the event collection for the given eventId\par If bookings are found, it should return the same bookings array\par Else it should return null\par\pard\f1\fs20\b eventBookingDb.updateBooking():\b (to be implemented)\par This method should take bookingId and quantity as parameters and update the booking details for the customer and do the other necessary changes in the customer and event collection\par A connection should be established to the database by invoking the getEventCollection method of the connection object\par It should update the quantity for the given bookingId by adding the given quantity, also reduce the available seats accordingly\par Also update the bookingCost for the booking by adding the required fare for the given quantity (additionalCost = pricePerTicket * quantity)\par Note: Get basePricePerSeat and eventDate from the event object, and seatZone from the existing booking to compute pricePerTicket (see Pricing Formula section)\par If bookingCost is successfully updated, it should update the wallet amount by subtracting the additional cost for the customer corresponding to the booking\par If wallet amount gets updated it should return the updated event details by invoking checkAvailability method of eventBookingDb object\par Else, it should return null\par\pard\f1\fs20\b service/events.js\b (partially implemented)\par Import all the required modules\par eBookingService object is created with the following methods:\par\bullet bookTickets()\par\bullet getAllBookings()\par\bullet customerBookingsByEvent()\par\bullet getBookingsByEventId()\par\bullet updateBooking()\par Note: Details of above methods are given below\par Finally, it should export eBookingService as a module\par\pard\f1\fs20\b eBookingService.bookTickets():\b (to be implemented)\par This method should take an eventBooking object as a parameter and book the mentioned quantity of tickets for an existing Event\par It should validate the eventId by invoking the validateEventId method of Validator.js\par It should validate the seatZone by invoking the validateSeatZone method of Validator.js\par It should invoke the checkCustomer method of eventBookingDb object by passing the customerId entered by the customer as a parameter which in turn returns customer details from the Customer collection\par If returned value is null, it should throw an error with message "Customer not registered. Register to proceed" and status as 404\par Else, it should invoke checkAvailability method of eventBookingDb object by passing the eventId entered by the user as a parameter which in turn returns event details from the Event collection\par If the returned value is null, it should throw an error with message "Event Unavailable" after setting error status 404\par If the status of the returned event is "Cancelled", it should throw an error with message "Sorry for the Inconvinience... <<eventId>> is cancelled!!" after setting error status 400\par If the status of the returned event is "Expired" or the eventDate is not in the future, it should throw an error with message "Event <<eventId>> has already expired!!" after setting error status 400\par If the availableSeats of the returned event is 0, it should throw an error with message "Event <<eventId>> is already full!!" after setting error status as 406\par If the availableSeats of the returned event is less than the required quantity, it should throw an error with message "Event almost Full... Only <<availableSeats>> left!!" after setting error status as 406\par Else, it should assign the bookingCost value to the EventBooking object (bookingCost = quantity * basePricePerSeat * seatZoneMultiplier * weekendSurcharge, see Pricing Formula section)\par It should then check if the available wallet amount is sufficient for booking or not\par If not, it should throw an error with message "Insufficient Wallet Amount. Add more Rs. <<amountNeeded>> to continue booking" after setting error status as 406\par Else, it should invoke the bookTickets method of eventBookingDb object which in turn returns the bookingId\par Finally, it should return the same bookingId\par\pard\f1\fs20\b eBookingService.getAllBookings():\b (to be implemented)\par This method should not take any parameter and return all the bookings over all the events\par It should invoke the getAllBookings() method of eventBookingDb object which in turn returns the array of booking details of all the events\par If the returned value is null, it should throw an error with message "No Bookings is found in any event" after setting error status as 404\par Else, it should return the same array of bookings\par\pard\f1\fs20\b eBookingService.customerBookingsByEvent():\b (to be implemented)\par This method should take customerId and eventId and return the corresponding customer booking details in the given event\par It should invoke the checkCustomer method of eventBookingDb object by passing customerId as parameter, which in turn returns the customer details\par If the returned value is null, it should throw an error with message "Customer not found" and status 404\par Else, it should invoke the checkAvailability method of eventBookingDb by passing eventId as parameter, which in turn returns the corresponding event details\par If the returned value is null, it should throw an error with message "Event detail not found" after setting error status as 404\par Else, it should invoke the customerBookingsByEvent() method of eventBookingDb by passing customerId and eventId as parameter which in turn returns the booking details for a customer in the given eventId\par If the returned value is null, it should throw an error with message "No Bookings found for <<customerId>> in <<eventId>>" after setting error status as 404\par Else, it should return the same booking details array\par\pard\f1\fs20\b eBookingService.getBookingsByEventId():\b (to be implemented)\par This method should take eventId as a parameter and return all the bookings done in that event\par It should invoke the getBookingsByEventId of eventBookingDb by passing eventId which in turn returns the array of booking objects or null\par If the returned value is null, it should throw an error with message "No Bookings found in <<eventId>>" after setting error status as 404\par Else, it should return the same booking details array\par\pard\f1\fs20\b eBookingService.updateBooking():\b (to be implemented)\par This method should take bookingId and quantity and update the corresponding booking\par It should invoke the checkBooking method of eventBookingDb object by passing bookingId as parameter, which in turn returns the event object or null\par If the returned value is null, it should throw an error with message "No Bookings with bookingId <<bookingId>>" after setting the appropriate error status\par If the status of returned event is "Cancelled", it should throw an error with message "Sorry for the Inconvenience... <<eventId>> has been cancelled!!" after setting the error status as 406\par If the status of the returned event is "Expired", it should throw an error with message "Sorry for the Inconvenience... <<eventId>> has already expired!!" after setting the error status as 406\par If the availableSeats of returned event is 0, it should throw an error with message "Event is already Full. Can't Book more tickets", after setting the error status as 406\par If the availableSeats of returned event is less than the required quantity, it should throw an error with message "Event almost Full. Only <<availableSeats>> seat left", after setting the error status as 406\par Else, it should check if the customer has sufficient walletAmount to book the required quantity by invoking checkCustomer method of eventBookingDb object\par If wallet amount is less, it should throw an error with message "Insufficient Wallet Amount. Add more Rs. <<amountNeeded>> to continue booking" after setting error status as 406\par Else, it should invoke updateBooking() method of eventBookingDb object by passing bookingId and quantity which in turn returns the updated event details, return the same\par If the returned value is null, it should throw an error with message "update failed" after setting error status as 502\par\pard\f1\fs20\b routing.js:\b (to be implemented)\par Import all required modules\par The following URI's should be configured for booking, fetching details & updating bookings respectively\par\pard\f1\fs20\b URI:- /bookTickets\par Configure the instance of Router, to handle the POST request for the given URI\par Once the request is received, it should create and populate an EventBooking object with the values present inside the request body\par It should invoke bookTickets method of eBookingService by passing the EventBooking object, which in turn returns bookingId wrapped inside a promise\par If the promise is successful it should populate the JSON response in the given format: {"message": "Event ticket booking is successful with booking Id: <<bookingId>>"} with status as 201\par Else if the promise fails, it should forward the control to next handler by passing the error object as parameter\par\pard\f1\fs20\b URI:- /getAllBookings\par Configure the instance of Router, in order to handle the GET request for the given URI\par It should invoke getAllBookings method of eBookingService, which in turn returns an array of booking objects\par If the promise is successful it should populate the JSON response with the bookings returned by the getAllBookings of eBookingService\par Else if the promise is failed it should forward the control to next handler by passing the error object as parameter\par\pard\f1\fs20\b URI:- /customerBookings/:customerId/:eventId\par It should also configure the instance of Router, to handle the GET request for the given URI\par It should invoke customerBookingsByEvent of eBookingService object by passing the customerId and eventId obtained from the URL, which in turn returns an array of bookings done by the customer for the given eventId\par If the promise is successful it should populate the JSON response with the bookings returned by the customerBookingsByEvent of eBookingService\par Else if the promise is failed it should forward the control to next handler by passing the error object as parameter\par\pard\f1\fs20\b URI:- /bookingsByEvent/:eventId\par It should also configure the instance of Router, to handle the GET request for the given URI\par It should invoke getBookingsByEventId of eBookingService object by passing the eventId, which in turn returns array of bookings done for that event\par If the promise is successful it should populate the JSON response with the bookings returned by the getBookingsByEventId of eBookingService\par Else if the promise is failed it should forward the control to next handler by passing the error object as parameter\par\pard\f1\fs20\b URI:- /updateBooking/:bookingId\par It should also configure the instance of Router, in order to handle the PUT request for the given URI\par It should invoke updateBooking() of eBookingService object by passing the bookingId obtained from the URL and quantity from the request body, which in turn returns an event object\par If the promise is successful it should populate the JSON response in the given format: {"message": "Booking successfully updated!! updated event details <<event>>"}\par Else if the promise fails, it should forward the control to next handler by passing the error object as parameter\par\pard\f1\fs20\b app.js:\b (To be implemented)\par All the required modules should be imported\par Middleware's should be organized properly for their appropriate functionality, in the order: body-parser, requestLogger, router, errorLogger\par The application should listen to requests coming through port 1060\par\pard\f1\fs20\b Pricing Formula\b (used in eBookingService.bookTickets and eBookingService.updateBooking):\par pricePerTicket = basePricePerSeat x seatZoneMultiplier x weekendSurcharge\par bookingCost    = quantity x pricePerTicket\par\pard\f1\fs20 Seat Zone Multipliers: VIP = 1.5, Standard = 1.0, Economy = 0.7\par Weekend Surcharge: if eventDate falls on a Saturday or Sunday, surcharge = 1.25, else 1.0\par (use new Date(eventDate).getDay(), where 0 = Sunday and 6 = Saturday)\par\pard\f1\fs20 Example: VIP seat, basePricePerSeat 200, weekend event, quantity 2\par => 200 x 1.5 x 1.25 x 2 = 750\par\pard\f1\fs26\b\par ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~All The Best~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\par\pard\f1\fs20\par\par}